      "type": "textEditor",
      "data": {
        "value": "<p><strong>PORPHYRIA PROFILE AND PBG URINE , 24 HRS</strong></p>\n<table class=\"MsoTableGrid\" border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"0\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Investigation</td>\n<td>Observation Value</td>\n<td>Unit</td>\n<td>Biological Reference Interval</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Porphyria Profile<br>(Urine 24 H )</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Porphobilinogen (Quantitative) , Urine</td>\n<td>0.57</td>\n<td>mg/24 hrs</td>\n<td>0 &ndash; 3.4</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Amino leveulinic acid, Urine</td>\n<td><strong>0.52</strong></td>\n<td>mg/24 hrs</td>\n<td>1 &ndash; 7 .0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"4\">Medical Remarks &ndash; Correlation with clinical history suggested.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Method: Columm Chromatography</p>\n<p><strong>Interpretation :</strong><br><strong>Methodology :</strong>Chromatography/spectrophotometry<br><strong>USES </strong><br>This test detects porphyrias and porphyrinurias. Acute intermittent porphyria is characterized by excretion of porphobilinogen and &Delta;-aminolevulinic acid in urine during acute attacks but not during latency.<br><br>This is appropriate test to rule out acute intermittent porphyria (AIP) and other acute attack types of porphyrias associated with neurologic and/or psychiatric symptoms.<br><br><strong>Limitations</strong><br><br>A 24-hour urine collection may provide more clinically representative data.</p>",
        "field": "textEditor"
      },
      "_id": "679c86d9a5b8d9a1e0d4150f"
    }
